    {
      "title": "PDUs and Encapsulation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "PDUs and Encapsulation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. PDU Names and Header Fields",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Layer",
                "PDU",
                "Header fields"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "L7-L5",
                  "data / message",
                  "none to know"
                ],
                [
                  "L4",
                  "segment (TCP), datagram (UDP)",
                  "source/destination `port`"
                ],
                [
                  "L3",
                  "packet",
                  "source/destination `IP`, `TTL`"
                ],
                [
                  "L2",
                  "frame",
                  "source/destination `MAC`, `EtherType`"
                ],
                [
                  "L1",
                  "bits",
                  "signals only"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Encapsulation and De-encapsulation",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Data",
                    "sub": "L7-L5",
                    "ink": "black"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "+ TCP header",
                    "sub": "segment",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "+ IP header",
                    "sub": "packet",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "+ Eth header + FCS",
                    "sub": "frame",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sender ==encapsulates downward==, each layer wraps the payload from above",
                "Receiver ==de-encapsulates upward==: each layer strips and reads its own header, then hands the payload up",
                "Only ==Data Link== adds a **trailer** (FCS); all other layers add headers only"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Trailer",
              "text": "Only the **frame** has a trailer: the ==FCS== at the end. Segments and packets have headers only."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Which layer adds a trailer?** Data Link only, the FCS.",
                "**What does a receiver do with a frame?** Each layer strips and reads its header, then passes the payload up.",
                "**Segment vs datagram?** Segment is TCP, datagram is UDP; both are L4.",
                "**Which fields does L3 read?** Source/destination IP and TTL."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
